Third-party material that is incorporated or closely followed:

* Lighting model (fieldform-gpu/src/shade.wgsl, flake.rs, environment.rs): the physically based
  equations follow Google Filament (https://github.com/google/filament), which is licensed under
  the Apache License 2.0. Where code or constants are carried over from it, they remain under that
  licence.
* Glossy reflections (fieldform-gpu/src/camera.wgsl, `reflected_direction`): the GGX visible-normal
  sampler follows E. Heitz, "Sampling the GGX Distribution of Visible Normals", Journal of Computer
  Graphics Techniques 7(4), 2018, as published; no code is carried over.
* Sharp creases on a cage (fieldform-subd/src/lib.rs `subdivide`, patch.rs): the crease rules follow
  H. Hoppe et al., "Piecewise Smooth Surface Reconstruction", SIGGRAPH 1994, and T. DeRose, M. Kass
  and T. Truong, "Subdivision Surfaces in Character Animation", SIGGRAPH 1998, as published; no code
  is carried over.
* Block-family colour check (tools/design/family_palette_check.py): the colour-vision simulation
  follows G. M. Machado, M. M. Oliveira and L. A. F. Fernandes, "A Physiologically-based Model for
  Simulation of Color Vision Deficiency", IEEE Transactions on Visualization and Computer Graphics
  15(6), 2009 (its severity-1.0 matrices); the colour difference is CIEDE2000 (CIE 142-2001).
* Vendored sources, each under its own licence and kept unmodified: Fidget (vendor/fidget, MPL-2.0)
  and the OpenCASCADE bindings (vendor/opencascade-rs, LGPL-2.1). The STEP importer links
  OpenCASCADE Technology (LGPL-2.1 with the OCCT exception) and runs as its own process.
* The application bundles egui's default fonts (MIT/Apache-2.0, OFL-1.1, Ubuntu Font Licence 1.0).
